WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.755
- Good morning Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:01.755 --> 00:00:02.962
My one word is believe,

00:00:02.962 --> 00:00:05.293
and I believe that you
have something special

00:00:05.293 --> 00:00:06.910
that when you unleash it,

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.811
it will be able to change the world.

00:00:08.811 --> 00:00:09.984
So to help you on your journey

00:00:09.984 --> 00:00:13.234
today's message is
outwork the competition.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.714
Over to you, Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson.

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.023
(Rooster crowing)

00:00:18.023 --> 00:00:20.574
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:20.574 --> 00:00:23.166
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:23.166 --> 00:00:27.359
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:29.008
- Yes, I get up at crazy hours.

00:00:29.008 --> 00:00:30.091
Whether it's three o'clock in the morning,

00:00:30.091 --> 00:00:31.340
by the way, when we were talking in London

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.518
I was getting up at three,

00:00:32.518 --> 00:00:34.307
'cause I had to be on the set by four,

00:00:34.307 --> 00:00:35.943
I'm sorry, by seven.

00:00:35.943 --> 00:00:38.826
So, whatever time my call time is,

00:00:38.826 --> 00:00:40.422
and I tell this to studios,

00:00:40.422 --> 00:00:42.008
and directors, and my producers,

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:42.964
whatever time my call time--

00:00:42.964 --> 00:00:45.271
so if my call time is at seven,

00:00:45.271 --> 00:00:47.737
then you back your clock up four hours,

00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:49.048
and then that's when I get up,

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.311
and train twice.

00:00:50.311 --> 00:00:51.777
I get my cardio in, then breakfast,

00:00:51.777 --> 00:00:53.474
and then I'll go hit the weights.

00:00:53.474 --> 00:00:57.438
Clanging and banging we
call it, jacking iron.

00:00:57.438 --> 00:00:58.862
- But what time do you go to bed?

00:00:58.862 --> 00:01:01.331
I mean, you might shoot
really late at night.

00:01:01.331 --> 00:01:02.302
- I'm averaging on,

00:01:02.302 --> 00:01:05.871
a movie I'll average probably
about five hours of sleep.

00:01:05.871 --> 00:01:08.731
All right empty gym, the way we like it.

00:01:08.731 --> 00:01:09.982
It's Sunday,

00:01:09.982 --> 00:01:11.658
just finished my warm up.

00:01:11.658 --> 00:01:12.590
It is family day,

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:13.423
it's the Lord's day,

00:01:13.423 --> 00:01:15.837
it is also leg day.

00:01:15.837 --> 00:01:17.837
So, this may not be fun.

00:01:19.323 --> 00:01:20.262
Happy Sunday.

00:01:20.262 --> 00:01:22.081
All right Saturday afternoon,

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.060
empty gym, the way we like it.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:24.893
I'm tripping over here.

00:01:24.893 --> 00:01:25.890
It's leg day,

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.882
which means it's going to be sweaty,

00:01:28.882 --> 00:01:30.215
painful and fun.

00:01:33.727 --> 00:01:34.560
Focus!

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:49.423
- [Cameraman] Come on, get it.

00:01:49.423 --> 00:01:50.256
Come on.

00:01:51.866 --> 00:01:53.449
Four left, come on.

00:01:56.575 --> 00:01:58.908
One more, come on. Up. Good.

00:02:02.126 --> 00:02:02.959
- Focus!

00:02:12.862 --> 00:02:14.342
All right workout number two.

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:16.462
I'm outworking all my competition.

00:02:16.462 --> 00:02:20.149
All right empty gym, the way we like it.

00:02:20.149 --> 00:02:21.570
Gettin' ready to get after it,

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.570
me and my favorite training partner.

00:02:26.338 --> 00:02:27.838
Let's bring it on!

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.683
(laughing)

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.516
Let's bring it on.

00:02:31.516 --> 00:02:32.349
- I love the rock.

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:34.604
I love his drive, I love his
motivation, love his ambition,

00:02:34.604 --> 00:02:36.160
I love his work ethic.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.141
There are two things that I
took from this video clip.

00:02:38.141 --> 00:02:40.282
One is you have to find
the work that you love.

00:02:40.282 --> 00:02:42.076
If you look at "The Rock",
you watch the video,

00:02:42.076 --> 00:02:43.775
he's working out Saturday,

00:02:43.775 --> 00:02:44.835
he's working out Sunday,

00:02:44.835 --> 00:02:46.503
he loves it when the gym is empty,

00:02:46.503 --> 00:02:48.110
he's outworking his competition.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.086
And that's incredibly
motivational to watch.

00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:51.832
You see him liftin' the weights and

00:02:51.832 --> 00:02:53.202
it gets you pumped up.

00:02:53.202 --> 00:02:55.703
But you should be doing the
same thing in your business.

00:02:55.703 --> 00:02:56.589
It doesn't mean you have to go

00:02:56.589 --> 00:02:58.363
and work out on a Saturday morning,

00:02:58.363 --> 00:03:00.143
but you should have
that same level of care,

00:03:00.143 --> 00:03:02.409
attention to detail, love, passion,

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:04.731
that he has for working out

00:03:04.731 --> 00:03:06.447
in your business.

00:03:06.447 --> 00:03:07.793
So if I look at what I do,

00:03:07.793 --> 00:03:10.677
I look at my YouTube channel everyday.

00:03:10.677 --> 00:03:12.538
I look at the comments,
I look at the stats,

00:03:12.538 --> 00:03:14.497
I look at the videos,

00:03:14.497 --> 00:03:16.237
the reactions that are coming in,

00:03:16.237 --> 00:03:17.892
I look at TDS stuff

00:03:17.892 --> 00:03:19.177
everyday,

00:03:19.177 --> 00:03:21.021
I look at what Lily's working on,

00:03:21.021 --> 00:03:22.768
I look at my website.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.749
I love the stuff that I'm doing

00:03:24.749 --> 00:03:28.603
where if it's a Saturday
morning and I'm waking up,

00:03:28.603 --> 00:03:30.355
and yes, I'm spending time with Hayden,

00:03:30.355 --> 00:03:32.054
and yes, I'm spending time with Nina,

00:03:32.054 --> 00:03:33.560
and yes, we're doing family activities

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.915
and barbecues and that kind of stuff.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.089
And I'm not spending as much time

00:03:38.089 --> 00:03:40.742
on a weekend as I am during the week

00:03:40.742 --> 00:03:42.204
on my business in the grind

00:03:42.204 --> 00:03:43.425
and everything that I'm doing there.

00:03:43.425 --> 00:03:44.628
But I'm still...

00:03:44.628 --> 00:03:46.336
It doesn't feel like work.

00:03:46.336 --> 00:03:48.068
I want to know what you guys are saying.

00:03:48.068 --> 00:03:49.491
I want to know what the
comments are coming in.

00:03:49.491 --> 00:03:51.619
I'm looking forward to
the life changing comment,

00:03:51.619 --> 00:03:52.625
everyone that comes in.

00:03:52.625 --> 00:03:54.978
I want to know how well
this new video series

00:03:54.978 --> 00:03:56.072
that we put up is doing.

00:03:56.072 --> 00:03:57.766
I want to know how well TDS is doin'.

00:03:57.766 --> 00:03:59.868
I want to know how well that
class we posted is doing.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:02.862
Did that marketing technique
work versus that technique?

00:04:02.862 --> 00:04:05.684
Or that slogan versus that slogan?

00:04:05.684 --> 00:04:07.372
How is everything working? I want to know.

00:04:07.372 --> 00:04:09.347
It fuels me, it gets me excited.

00:04:09.347 --> 00:04:10.475
It's not work.

00:04:10.475 --> 00:04:12.109
It's not waking up on Saturday like

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:13.921
"Ah, I got to check my

00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:16.378
"stupid YouTube comments. These people!"

00:04:16.378 --> 00:04:18.457
All right, it's not like that, I love it.

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:21.703
It's finding that thing
that you love doing,

00:04:21.703 --> 00:04:22.880
and this is a consistent message

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.666
across everybody pretty
much that we profile.

00:04:25.666 --> 00:04:27.738
You have to love the work so that

00:04:27.738 --> 00:04:28.958
waking up on a Saturday to go

00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:30.580
and do this thing whatever it is,

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.557
acting, working out,

00:04:32.557 --> 00:04:34.664
doing SEO, making videos,

00:04:34.664 --> 00:04:36.190
whatever it is,

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:37.721
you look forward to it.

00:04:37.721 --> 00:04:38.554
You want to do it.

00:04:38.554 --> 00:04:39.731
You're happy that you're there.

00:04:39.731 --> 00:04:41.510
You're not complaining that you should be

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.207
at this barbecue or you
should be sleeping in

00:04:44.207 --> 00:04:46.880
or you should be going to
watch that baseball game

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:47.713
or whatever it is,

00:04:47.713 --> 00:04:50.109
'cause you enjoy the work
of what you're doing.

00:04:50.109 --> 00:04:52.576
Having that level of
commitment and passion

00:04:52.576 --> 00:04:54.944
to the crap that you are focused on

00:04:54.944 --> 00:04:56.148
I think is really really important

00:04:56.148 --> 00:04:58.408
to have success in any field.

00:04:58.408 --> 00:05:00.086
The second thing that I
really took from this video

00:05:00.086 --> 00:05:01.974
is the importance of the morning routine.

00:05:01.974 --> 00:05:05.553
And what I found really
interesting was how,

00:05:05.553 --> 00:05:06.880
if he was on shoot,

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.340
and he knows he needs x number of hours,

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:12.161
he would wake up those
number of hours early

00:05:12.161 --> 00:05:14.341
to then make sure he
does his morning routine,

00:05:14.341 --> 00:05:17.674
and being fanatical about
keeping that morning routine.

00:05:17.674 --> 00:05:19.935
I'm a big believer in
having a morning routine.

00:05:19.935 --> 00:05:21.839
I think it really sets you up for success.

00:05:21.839 --> 00:05:23.301
If you find the thing that makes you feel

00:05:23.301 --> 00:05:25.642
bold and confident and alive and excited,

00:05:25.642 --> 00:05:27.627
and put that into your morning routine,

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.910
then you're much more likely
to have an amazing day

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.174
instead of randomly hoping

00:05:31.174 --> 00:05:33.009
you get inspired throughout the day.

00:05:33.009 --> 00:05:34.110
Most people fall out of bed

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.395
and just do a couple things

00:05:35.395 --> 00:05:37.024
and then they're off to work.

00:05:37.024 --> 00:05:38.592
Kind of going through the motions

00:05:38.592 --> 00:05:40.915
as opposed to having
designed a morning routine

00:05:40.915 --> 00:05:42.399
to really support you.

00:05:42.399 --> 00:05:44.045
For me, I find myself--

00:05:44.045 --> 00:05:45.712
If I get distracted,

00:05:46.807 --> 00:05:49.281
I fall off the morning routine,

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:50.789
I fall off my schedule.

00:05:50.789 --> 00:05:52.137
So the key for me, traditionally,

00:05:52.137 --> 00:05:54.288
has been to eliminate distractions.

00:05:54.288 --> 00:05:55.556
It's why I don't use a cell phone.

00:05:55.556 --> 00:05:57.060
It's why I have a rigid schedule.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.313
It's why I don't have a number
that you can call me on.

00:05:59.313 --> 00:06:02.545
It's why I have certain
days for different things.

00:06:02.545 --> 00:06:04.837
But, if I'm traveling,

00:06:04.837 --> 00:06:06.960
or if something else
is kind of falling off,

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.426
I'm committed somewhere that's
a little strange for me,

00:06:10.426 --> 00:06:12.375
it's not part of my usual routine,

00:06:12.375 --> 00:06:14.086
then I don't do my morning routine

00:06:14.086 --> 00:06:15.913
or I'm not as consistent with it.

00:06:15.913 --> 00:06:18.057
So that's an area that
I could be better at.

00:06:18.057 --> 00:06:19.385
I think, even today,

00:06:19.385 --> 00:06:21.969
I watched the "The Rock" video yesterday,

00:06:21.969 --> 00:06:23.321
and so today I did.

00:06:23.321 --> 00:06:25.116
Today is filming day for me.

00:06:25.116 --> 00:06:27.403
So I'm coming in, we
have to be here at 8:30.

00:06:27.403 --> 00:06:28.969
We start filming,

00:06:28.969 --> 00:06:32.386
and we're going to make
60, 70 videos today.

00:06:33.832 --> 00:06:35.535
If I woke up when I normally woke up

00:06:35.535 --> 00:06:37.991
then I wouldn't have time
to do my morning routine.

00:06:37.991 --> 00:06:39.479
So I woke up earlier today.

00:06:39.479 --> 00:06:40.752
Woke up a little bit earlier,

00:06:40.752 --> 00:06:41.585
I went through everything

00:06:41.585 --> 00:06:43.163
that I normally do on a morning routine,

00:06:43.163 --> 00:06:44.543
and I feel great, and I'm here,

00:06:44.543 --> 00:06:45.822
ready to record for you.

00:06:45.822 --> 00:06:48.651
This is a weird day for me
'cause this happens once a month.

00:06:48.651 --> 00:06:50.825
It throws off my schedule.

00:06:50.825 --> 00:06:54.878
I think that strategy of trying
to eliminate distractions,

00:06:54.878 --> 00:06:57.998
eliminate schedule
changes can really help.

00:06:57.998 --> 00:07:00.231
It really adds a lot of value to me.

00:07:00.231 --> 00:07:02.762
And on 90% of the days

00:07:02.762 --> 00:07:04.718
it works because I
don't have distractions,

00:07:04.718 --> 00:07:06.000
I've eliminated from them,

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.305
my team knows not to distract me

00:07:07.305 --> 00:07:08.883
unless it's really important,

00:07:08.883 --> 00:07:11.748
cut out all the things
that were taking attention

00:07:11.748 --> 00:07:13.801
away from me being able to
focus on what I'm doing.

00:07:13.801 --> 00:07:15.958
But for those 10% of the days,

00:07:15.958 --> 00:07:18.353
it's an interesting strategy.

00:07:18.353 --> 00:07:20.179
When something unexpected happens

00:07:20.179 --> 00:07:21.497
or when I'm traveling

00:07:21.497 --> 00:07:24.391
or when I have to wake
up to come to do this

00:07:24.391 --> 00:07:26.230
or something like that.

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.322
The idea of waking up earlier and making

00:07:28.322 --> 00:07:31.809
that morning routine an
absolute must 100% of the time,

00:07:31.809 --> 00:07:33.113
is something that I'm going to take away

00:07:33.113 --> 00:07:34.280
and maybe apply to my life.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:35.799
We'll see how it works out.

00:07:35.799 --> 00:07:37.606
So the question of today is, I'm curious,

00:07:37.606 --> 00:07:40.125
what is the most important
thing from your morning routine?

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:42.371
The thing that you know if
you did every single day

00:07:42.371 --> 00:07:44.153
you would set yourself
up for an amazing day.

00:07:44.153 --> 00:07:47.364
What is the one most important
part of your morning routine?

00:07:47.364 --> 00:07:48.539
I'd love to hear from you.

00:07:48.539 --> 00:07:49.930
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:50.763
I also want to give a quick

00:07:50.763 --> 00:07:51.806
shout out to Michael Johnson.

00:07:51.806 --> 00:07:52.878
Michael thank you so much

00:07:52.878 --> 00:07:54.602
for picking up a copy
of my book Your One Word

00:07:54.602 --> 00:07:56.706
and posting a picture on Instagram,

00:07:56.706 --> 00:07:57.696
I love the smile.

00:07:57.696 --> 00:07:58.966
Thank you so much for the support,

00:07:58.966 --> 00:08:00.227
I really appreciate it

00:08:00.227 --> 00:08:01.731
and I'm so glad you enjoyed the read.

00:08:01.731 --> 00:08:02.994
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:08:02.994 --> 00:08:04.217
I believe in you.

00:08:04.217 --> 00:08:06.140
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.216
and whatever your one word is.

00:08:08.216 --> 00:08:11.059
Much love, and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:08:11.059 --> 00:08:13.845
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:08:13.845 --> 00:08:16.313
♫ I wake up every morning

00:08:16.313 --> 00:08:19.730
♫ espresso keep me going

00:08:22.784 --> 00:08:25.830
- The choice you have as an underdog is

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:28.255
if you're going to choose to fight

00:08:28.255 --> 00:08:31.263
and choose to fight to win,

00:08:31.263 --> 00:08:33.692
there are a series of
strategies available to you,

00:08:33.692 --> 00:08:35.862
but they are all more costly

00:08:35.862 --> 00:08:38.662
than the strategies
available to the favorite.

00:08:38.662 --> 00:08:41.745
I give the example of a chapter about

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.113
a software mogul in Silicone Valley,

00:08:45.113 --> 00:08:47.847
an Indian guy, who
coaches his daughter's--

00:08:47.847 --> 00:08:51.113
12 year old daughter's basketball team.

00:08:51.113 --> 00:08:53.113
They are without talent.

00:08:56.151 --> 00:08:59.095
By his own admission, they didn't --

00:08:59.095 --> 00:09:00.187
barely knew how to play the game.

00:09:00.187 --> 00:09:02.834
He takes them all way to
the National Championships.

00:09:02.834 --> 00:09:04.549
He does it by,

00:09:04.549 --> 00:09:05.893
he instructs them they're going to play

00:09:05.893 --> 00:09:09.401
the full-court press
every minute of every game

00:09:09.401 --> 00:09:12.318
and defend every inch of the court.

00:09:13.479 --> 00:09:16.057
That's actually a very effective strategy.

00:09:16.057 --> 00:09:19.140
Particularly in age class basketball.

00:09:20.078 --> 00:09:21.410
If you're the underdog,

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:22.733
it's really your only chance of winning

00:09:22.733 --> 00:09:24.676
is to play a really
really aggressive defense.

00:09:24.676 --> 00:09:26.496
It requires, however,

00:09:26.496 --> 00:09:28.371
that everyone on your team

00:09:28.371 --> 00:09:30.907
expend maximum effort

00:09:30.907 --> 00:09:32.693
every minute of the game.

00:09:32.693 --> 00:09:35.870
You cannot loaf for an instant.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:37.397
You have to be in really good shape

00:09:37.397 --> 00:09:39.270
and you have to run yourself ragged

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.759
and you cannot let up.

00:09:40.759 --> 00:09:42.541
Most people will not play that way

00:09:42.541 --> 00:09:45.021
because it's too difficult.

00:09:45.021 --> 00:09:48.045
If I said to you "We're
not going to be doing

00:09:48.045 --> 00:09:49.397
"elegantly designed plays

00:09:49.397 --> 00:09:51.703
"and shooting gorgeous baskets

00:09:51.703 --> 00:09:53.314
"and passing the ball.

00:09:53.314 --> 00:09:55.273
"We're just going to be doing this

00:09:55.273 --> 00:09:56.450
"for the entire game

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.344
"and you're going to be
exhausted at the end."

00:09:58.344 --> 00:10:01.593
Most kids would say "That's
not why I signed up."

00:10:01.593 --> 00:10:04.228
That's a kind of classic illustration of

00:10:04.228 --> 00:10:05.228
that effort,

00:10:06.206 --> 00:10:07.934
effort is the root,

00:10:07.934 --> 00:10:10.009
one of the roots
available to the underdog,

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:11.509
I can outwork you.

00:10:12.615 --> 00:10:14.580
I may not be able to outspend you,

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.025
but I can outwork you.

00:10:16.025 --> 00:10:19.515
Well, outworking is a tall order.

00:10:19.515 --> 00:10:21.098
It's not easy to do

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:25.997
as anyone who has worked
in a start-up knows.

00:10:25.997 --> 00:10:29.186
That's one of the stressful parts of it.

00:10:29.186 --> 00:10:31.733
But successful start-ups,

00:10:31.733 --> 00:10:35.081
I've never seen any
actual data on this, but,

00:10:35.081 --> 00:10:37.163
do we think the people working for

00:10:37.163 --> 00:10:38.792
successful start-ups work longer hours

00:10:38.792 --> 00:10:41.583
than people who work
Fortune 500 companies?

00:10:41.583 --> 00:10:43.802
- But when you look at the
business that you're in,

00:10:43.802 --> 00:10:45.574
do you find that your hustle

00:10:45.574 --> 00:10:47.843
and your ability to outwork helps?

00:10:47.843 --> 00:10:49.230
- Absolutely.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:50.602
Absolutely.

00:10:50.602 --> 00:10:51.891
When I say that this business,

00:10:51.891 --> 00:10:54.774
and I learned this from Luther
Campbell from 2 Live Crew,

00:10:54.774 --> 00:10:57.228
one of the first guys I
did a record deal with,

00:10:57.228 --> 00:11:02.102
he always said that it's
90% business, 10% talent.

00:11:02.102 --> 00:11:03.625
And if you see that in the most--

00:11:03.625 --> 00:11:05.068
the ones that are the most talented

00:11:05.068 --> 00:11:06.982
are the hardest to
either get in the studio,

00:11:06.982 --> 00:11:08.354
or are the ones that get up on stage

00:11:08.354 --> 00:11:09.751
and they don't know if they're
going to hit the right note

00:11:09.751 --> 00:11:11.191
or if they're going to do this right.

00:11:11.191 --> 00:11:12.750
And I go "Hey don't
worry about it, come on,

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:13.583
"let's keep it moving baby!"
- [Ryan] Let's go!

00:11:13.583 --> 00:11:14.416
Let's hustle it up!

00:11:14.416 --> 00:11:15.365
- There's opportunities out here, man!

00:11:15.365 --> 00:11:16.946
Come on, man!

00:11:16.946 --> 00:11:18.959
- The next thing is,

00:11:18.959 --> 00:11:20.682
I would say

00:11:20.682 --> 00:11:21.625
the hard work.

00:11:21.625 --> 00:11:23.351
Hard work is really really important.

00:11:23.351 --> 00:11:24.990
To be successful,

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.657
and to be at the top

00:11:28.094 --> 00:11:31.111
10% of the population in terms of success,

00:11:31.111 --> 00:11:33.573
all those people worked their ass off.

00:11:33.573 --> 00:11:37.161
You're not going to be
successful without hard work.

00:11:37.161 --> 00:11:38.310
And the reason, mostly,

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:40.168
is not even that you have to go out there

00:11:40.168 --> 00:11:41.958
and build a giant empire,

00:11:41.958 --> 00:11:43.291
Or you have to--

00:11:44.239 --> 00:11:46.840
a mass amount of money or work long hours,

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:48.204
it's not even so much about that.

00:11:48.204 --> 00:11:50.335
It's that you need to develop yourself.

00:11:50.335 --> 00:11:53.918
Success is not so much
an outer world state

00:11:54.828 --> 00:11:56.738
as an inner world state.

00:11:56.738 --> 00:11:59.308
That might sound kind
of hokey and new age,

00:11:59.308 --> 00:12:01.181
but it's very very true.

00:12:01.181 --> 00:12:03.364
Success is grounded within you.

00:12:03.364 --> 00:12:04.746
You're not going to be able to maintain

00:12:04.746 --> 00:12:07.049
any sort of level of success

00:12:07.049 --> 00:12:10.275
if you do not have the psychology

00:12:10.275 --> 00:12:13.145
to really follow principles,

00:12:13.145 --> 00:12:15.774
to know how to maintain success,

00:12:15.774 --> 00:12:19.240
to think strategically,
to think long term,

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:23.121
to delay gratification,
to resist addictions.

00:12:23.121 --> 00:12:24.633
All of these factors come into play.

00:12:24.633 --> 00:12:25.684
So really, for me,

00:12:25.684 --> 00:12:27.899
success is grounded in self mastery.

00:12:27.899 --> 00:12:29.359
It's understanding yourself

00:12:29.359 --> 00:12:31.056
and then building on that.

00:12:31.056 --> 00:12:34.078
Building disciplines,
building successful habits,

00:12:34.078 --> 00:12:37.617
which then move you towards
where you want to be going.

